+++ b/.github/ci/platform-cases.tsv
@@ -105,6 +105,31 @@ internal/godriver	TestBuildFailsClosedWhenTheGoChildCannotStart	windows	darwin	p
 # Executable identity and executable behaviour
 # ===========================================================================
 internal/godriver	TestExecutableIdentityRejectsSubstitutionAndMutation	darwin,windows	-	-	the toolchain executable identity rejects substitution and mutation
+
+# The manager resolves its own executable to the canonical installed file
+# BEFORE the substitution battery above runs, so the launch shape an operator
+# used -- a shim link on PATH, a chain of them, a linked install directory, a
+# Windows directory junction -- is not itself a fault. That ordering is a
+# Windows-only behaviour change (`physicalPath` rather than
+# `filepath.EvalSymlinks`, which since Go 1.23 does not follow a junction), so
+# the two junction cases below are the only ones that catch a regression of it
+# and a runner must be REQUIRED to execute them by name.
+#
+# The tolerated skip is narrow and classified: creating a file symbolic link on
+# Windows needs SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege and creating a junction needs
+# `mklink /J` to work, neither of which a hosted runner is obliged to grant.
+# Every such skip is recorded in `skips-observed.tsv` against
+# `host-capability`, and a skip for any other reason -- or any skip at all on
+# darwin, which creates both -- is fatal.
+internal/godriver	TestExecutableIdentityResolvesALauncherLink	darwin,windows	windows	host-capability	the manager resolves its own executable through a package-manager launcher link, and every launch shape yields the one installed identity
+internal/godriver	TestExecutableIdentityResolvesALauncherLink/*	-	windows	host-capability	a launch-shape subtest may skip only where the Windows host forbids unprivileged symlink creation; the case itself must still pass
+internal/godriver	TestExecutableIdentityRejectsSubstitutionThroughALauncherLink	darwin,windows	windows	host-capability	resolving the launch shape does not trust what it reaches: substitution of the installed file still fails closed
+internal/godriver	TestExecutableIdentityRejectsSubstitutionThroughALauncherLink/*	-	windows	host-capability	a substitution subtest may skip only where the Windows host forbids unprivileged symlink creation; the case itself must still pass
+internal/godriver	TestExecutableIdentityResolvesARealSymlinkedProcessLaunch	darwin,windows	windows	host-capability	a process really started through a launcher link resolves the installed identity, so what os.Executable reports for this platform is observed rather than assumed
+internal/godriver	TestBuildAcceptsAManagerStartedThroughALauncherLink	darwin,windows	windows	host-capability	the whole identity handshake completes for a manager whose own path is a launcher link
+internal/godriver	TestWorkerProvesTheInstalledIdentityWhenLaunchedThroughALink	darwin,windows	windows	host-capability	a worker process started from a launcher link proves the installed identity back over the protocol
+internal/godriver	TestExecutableIdentityResolvesALauncherReachedThroughADirectoryJunction	windows	windows	host-capability	a manager installed under a directory junction resolves instead of being refused as a non-canonical file -- the shape EvalSymlinks alone cannot follow
+internal/godriver	TestExecutableIdentityStillRejectsSubstitutionBehindAJunction	windows	windows	host-capability	a retargeted, dangling or hard-linked install behind a junction cannot move a recorded manager identity or pass as it
 internal/runtimestore	TestUnixPostInstallShimPropagatesSignal	linux,darwin	-	-	the installed unix shim is executable and propagates signals
 internal/shell	TestPosixHookEntersNestedSwitchesAndLeavesProjects	linux,darwin	windows	platform-control	executes the POSIX shell hook end to end
 internal/shell	TestPowerShellHookRunsOnEveryPrompt	windows	linux,darwin	platform-control	executes the PowerShell prompt hook end to end
